{"call_id":"exec-73fb1851-4882-47a9-bc48-6acc15787a0e","node_id":"evaluate","output":" M harness/agy/adapter.go\n M harness/agy/adapter_test.go\n?? .tractor/\n?? WORK_SUMMARY.md\n?? ephemeral/worklog/202608191900-agy-artifact-prevention.md\n?? harness/agy/native_write_hook.go\n harness/agy/adapter.go      |  62 +++++++++++----\n harness/agy/adapter_test.go | 180 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 229 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)\nM\tharness/agy/adapter.go\nM\tharness/agy/adapter_test.go\n# agy artifact-path bug: preventive layer (round 1)\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThe task's hypothesized fix — a custom-agent `tools:` allowlist selected via\n`agy --agent \u003cname\u003e` — **does not work**. I proved this empirically with\nfive real `agy 1.1.15` invocations before writing any adapter code for it,\nthen pivoted to the mechanism that does work: a global `PreToolUse` deny\nhook (`hooks.json`), which is real, documented (inside the CLI binary\nitself), and verified live to block the broken tool call before it executes.\nIt does not eliminate the reactive repair-retry from `ae5edb6` — nothing I\nfound does, in agy 1.1.15's headless single-turn model — but it converts an\nagy-internal, version-fragile failure into a fast, deterministic,\nTractor-controlled one, and the existing repair-retry still recovers the\nturn exactly as before. Full reasoning and evidence:\n`ephemeral/worklog/202608191900-agy-artifact-prevention.md` (durable,\nsurvives the source research reports being deleted).\n\n## What I built\n\n- `harness/agy/native_write_hook.go` (new): idempotent, merge-safe\n  provisioning of a Tractor-owned `PreToolUse` hook entry in agy's global\n  `~/.gemini/config/hooks.json`, denying `write_to_file`,\n  `replace_file_content`, and `multi_replace_file_content` before they\n  execute. Collision-safe: refuses to overwrite a same-named hook that\n  lacks Tractor's marker string, rather than clobbering a user's own hook.\n- `harness/agy/adapter.go`: `ensureHook()` provisions the hook once per\n  `Adapter` (`sync.Once`) before the first `agy` invocation.\n  `isArtifactPathError` now also matches the hook's own denial text, so\n  the existing `ae5edb6` bounded repair-retry catches and recovers from it\n  identically to agy's native artifact-path error. `categorize()` gained a\n  `\"denied by pre-tool hook\"` terminal marker so a persistent denial (both\n  turns fail) is categorized `ErrorTerminal`, matching the existing\n  artifact-path behavior, not `ErrorRetryable`.\n- `runnerConfig` gained a `homeDir` override (empty = `os.UserHomeDir()`)\n  so tests never touch the real `~/.gemini`. **This was a real bug I found\n  and fixed in the test harness itself**: before this change, every\n  existing test that called `RunTurn`/`CreateSession` would have silently\n  provisioned into the developer's actual global agy config the first time\n  this feature landed and tests ran. `testAdapter` now always sets\n  `homeDir: t.TempDir()`.\n\n### What I deliberately did NOT build\n\nPer the task's own instruction to verify empirically rather than trust the\nreports: I built the `--agent` + custom-agent-manifest + `init.tools`\ninvariant-enforcement path first, then **tore it out** after proving live\nthat agy 1.1.15 does not honor a `mainAgent`'s `tools:` allowlist at all —\n`init.tools` reports the full 57-tool baseline regardless of the manifest\ncontent (tested down to a 1-tool allowlist), and an explicitly-excluded\n`write_to_file` remained fully callable and reproduced the original bug.\nShipping that code anyway would have been dead, misleading infrastructure —\nan `--agent` flag and an `init.tools` fail-fast check that either does\nnothing or (if implemented as literally specified: fail if `write_to_file`\nis advertised) would make **every single turn fail**, since that tool is\nalways advertised. Full evidence and the manifest shape (kept for future\nreference, in case a later agy version fixes this) is in the worklog.\n\n## Placement decision and tradeoffs\n\n**Global** (`~/.gemini/config/hooks.json`), not workspace-local\n(`\u003cworkdir\u003e/.agents/hooks.json`):\n\n- Tractor's isolated-worktree branches (`engine/artifacts.go`, `2485e4c`)\n  each get their own workdir. A workspace-local hook file would need\n  provisioning into and cleanup from every branch's worktree, and any file\n  left behind would show up in that branch's `git status` and risk being\n  swept into artifact collection — exactly what the task said to avoid.\n  A single global file, written once, sidesteps both.\n- Real tradeoff, accepted deliberately: the hook is global, so it also\n  denies native writes for the user's own manual interactive `agy\n  --add-dir \u003cworkspace\u003e` sessions, not just Tractor-launched ones. Since\n  the underlying bug isn't print-mode-specific, this is net-positive — it\n  fixes the same failure for their own usage too — but it is a real,\n  disclosed behavior change outside Tractor's own runs. Documented in the\n  worklog.\n- Idempotent and collision-safe: `ensureNativeWriteHook` merges into any\n  existing `hooks.json` (doesn't touch other keys), no-ops if its own key\n  already matches canonical content byte-for-byte, and errors out rather\n  than overwriting a same-named key that isn't Tractor's (no marker string\n  in its reason text).\n\n## Smoke-test evidence (5 real `agy 1.1.15` invocations, all under `timeout 120`)\n\n**1. Baseline, no `--agent`** — canonical `init.tools` (57 tools):\n\n```\nask_custom_permission, ask_permission, ask_question, browser_click_element,\nbrowser_drag_pixel_to_pixel, browser_get_dom, browser_get_network_request,\nbrowser_input, browser_list_network_requests, browser_mouse_down,\nbrowser_mouse_up, browser_move_mouse, browser_press_key,\nbrowser_refresh_page, browser_resize_window, browser_scroll,\nbrowser_scroll_dom, browser_select_option, browser_subagent, call_mcp_tool,\ncapture_browser_console_logs, capture_browser_screenshot,\nclick_browser_pixel, command_status, define_subagent, delete_knowledge,\nexecute_browser_javascript, find_by_name, finish, generate_image,\ngrep_search, invoke_subagent, list_browser_pages, list_dir,\nlist_permissions, list_resources, manage_inbox, manage_subagents,\nmanage_task, multi_replace_file_content, notebook_edit,\nnotebook_execution, open_browser_url, read_browser_page, read_resource,\nread_url_content, replace_file_content, run_command, schedule, search_web,\nsed_file, send_command_input, send_message, view_file, wait,\nwait_5_seconds, write_to_file\n```\n\n**2. `--agent` with a hand-authored manifest excluding the 3 native\nwriters** — `init.tools` was **byte-identical to the baseline above**,\n`write_to_file` included, regardless of the manifest. Forcing the model to\ncall `write_to_file` directly reproduced the original bug exactly:\n\n```\n\"error\":{\"type\":\"TOOL_ERROR\",\"message\":\"declaring permissions: cortex tool\nwrite_to_file: convert tool call for permissions: model output error:\ninvalid tool call error (invalid_args) /tmp/.../forced.txt is not a valid\nartifact path; artifacts must be in\n/Users/tyler/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/\u003cuuid\u003e/\"}\n```\n\nThis is the proof that the task's hypothesized mechanism doesn't work; see\nthe worklog for the two intermediate invocations (a too-literal manifest\nthat failed CLI-side \"not found in registry\" validation, and a 1-tool\nmanifest confirming `init.tools` never changes regardless of allowlist\ncontent).\n\n**3. Final invocation, using the actual Go-code-generated hook\n(`ensureNativeWriteHook` against the real `$HOME`, then cleaned up\nafterward)**, model instructed to call `write_to_file` directly and fall\nback on denial:\n\n```\n{\"tool_name\":\"write_to_file\",\"state\":\"ERROR\",\"error\":{\"type\":\"TOOL_ERROR\",\n \"message\":\"tool call denied by pre-tool hook: [tractor-no-native-write]\n Native write_to_file, replace_file_content, and multi_replace_file_content\n are disabled: ...\"}}\n{\"tool_name\":\"run_command\",\"state\":\"DONE\",\n \"parameters\":{\"CommandLine\":\"echo \\\"final check\\\" \u003e .../final.txt\"}}\n```\n\n`final.txt` was present on disk with the correct content afterward. The\ndenied `write_to_file` call never touched the filesystem; the model\nrecovered on its own via `run_command` within the same turn. (The overall\nturn `result.status` was still `ERROR` with the hook's denial as\n`result.error` — this is the \"does not eliminate the turn failure\" finding\ndocumented in the worklog; Tractor's `isArtifactPathError` /\n`artifactWriteRepairPrompt` repair-retry from `ae5edb6` is what actually\nrecovers a valid structured result on the next turn.)\n\nAll experimental global state (`~/.gemini/config/agents/tractor-shell-only*`,\n`~/.gemini/config/hooks.json`) was removed after each test; the developer's\nreal machine is back to its pre-work state. Tests never touch the real\n`~/.gemini` (`testAdapter` uses `homeDir: t.TempDir()`).\n\n## Test results\n\n```\n$ gofmt -l .\n(no output — clean)\n\n$ go vet ./...\n(no output — clean)\n\n$ go test ./harness/agy/... -v\n=== RUN   TestCreateSessionAndRunTurn\n--- PASS: TestCreateSessionAndRunTurn (0.02s)\n=== RUN   TestRunTurnReconstructsAndRejectsConversationMismatch\n--- PASS: TestRunTurnReconstructsAndRejectsConversationMismatch (0.01s)\n=== RUN   TestRunTurnRepairsAtMostOnce\n--- PASS: TestRunTurnRepairsAtMostOnce (0.01s)\n=== RUN   TestRunTurnRecoversFromArtifactPathError\n--- PASS: TestRunTurnRecoversFromArtifactPathError (0.01s)\n=== RUN   TestRunTurnArtifactPathErrorRepairsAtMostOnce\n--- PASS: TestRunTurnArtifactPathErrorRepairsAtMostOnce (0.01s)\n=== RUN   TestIsArtifactPathError (+ subtests, incl. hook-denial case)\n--- PASS: TestIsArtifactPathError (0.00s)\n=== RUN   TestRunTurnRecoversFromNativeWriteHookDenial\n--- PASS: TestRunTurnRecoversFromNativeWriteHookDenial (0.01s)\n=== RUN   TestRunTurnNativeWriteHookDenialRepairsAtMostOnce\n--- PASS: TestRunTurnNativeWriteHookDenialRepairsAtMostOnce (0.01s)\n=== RUN   TestEnsureNativeWriteHookIdempotentAndContentCorrect\n--- PASS: TestEnsureNativeWriteHookIdempotentAndContentCorrect (0.00s)\n=== RUN   TestEnsureNativeWriteHookMergesWithExistingHooks\n--- PASS: TestEnsureNativeWriteHookMergesWithExistingHooks (0.00s)\n=== RUN   TestEnsureNativeWriteHookRefusesForeignEntry\n--- PASS: TestEnsureNativeWriteHookRefusesForeignEntry (0.00s)\n=== RUN   TestAdapterProvisionsHookBeforeFirstInvocation\n--- PASS: TestAdapterProvisionsHookBeforeFirstInvocation (0.00s)\n(... all other pre-existing tests unchanged and passing ...)\nPASS\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/harness/agy\t0.482s\n\n$ go test ./...\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/cmd/agent\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/cmd/tractor\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/engine\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/examples\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/graph\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/harness\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/harness/agy\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/harness/claude\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/harness/codex\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/internal/runlog\nok  \tgithub.com/tylergannon/tractor/lint\n```\n\n## Files changed\n\n- `harness/agy/native_write_hook.go` — new; the hook mechanism.\n- `harness/agy/adapter.go` — `ensureHook()` wiring, `isArtifactPathError`\n  now matches the hook's denial too, `categorize()` gained a terminal\n  marker for hook denials, `runnerConfig.homeDir`.\n- `harness/agy/adapter_test.go` — new tests (hook idempotency/content,\n  merge-safety, collision refusal, provisioning-before-first-invocation,\n  repair-retry via hook denial) plus the `homeDir: t.TempDir()` fix so\n  existing tests stop touching the real `~/.gemini`.\n- `ephemeral/worklog/202608191900-agy-artifact-prevention.md` — durable\n  distillation (failure mechanism, why config/flags don't fix it, why the\n  `tools:` allowlist doesn't work with hard evidence, the hook mechanism,\n  version constraints, upstream bug reports to file).\n\nNo files under the main checkout (`/Users/tyler/src/tractor`) were touched.\nNothing committed.\nephemeral/worklog/202608161810-initialize-project.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608161836-implement-attractor.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608162121-independent-cli-validation.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608162136-build-orchestration.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608170023-independent-agent-validation.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608170739-live-examples.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608170900-yaml-input.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608171110-generated-yaml.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608171707-spec-supervisors.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608171718-tractor-mcp-plugin.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608171911-release-skill.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608172021-public-mit.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608172034-normalize-plugin-install.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608172059-detached-mcp-runs.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608180724-attractor-reference.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608181244-agy-harness-adapter.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608181330-agy-steering-compaction.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608181734-release-v0.3.0.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608181820-heterogeneous-fanout-workspaces.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608182048-docs-plugin-refresh.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608191356-agy-artifact-validator.md\nephemeral/worklog/202608191900-agy-artifact-prevention.md\nephemeral/worklog/tractor-docs-site.md\nephemeral/reviews/202608161906-tractor-design-round-01.md\nephemeral/reviews/202608161916-tractor-design-round-02.md\nephemeral/reviews/202608161924-tractor-design-round-03.md\nephemeral/reviews/202608161936-tractor-design-round-04.md\nephemeral/reviews/202608161945-tractor-design-round-05.md\nephemeral/reviews/202608161953-tractor-design-round-06.md\nephemeral/reviews/202608162105-implementation-round-01.md\nephemeral/reviews/202608162105-implementation-round-02.md\nephemeral/reviews/202608162145-orchestration-plan-round-01.md\nephemeral/reviews/202608162155-orchestration-plan-round-02.md\n