{"args":{"content":"package agy\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n)\n\n// TractorAgentName is the agy custom-agent Tractor provisions and selects\n// with `--agent` on every invocation. Selecting it removes agy's native\n// file-write tools from the model's toolset entirely, so the model can\n// never reach the artifact-path validator that fails a turn after a\n// successful workspace write (see nativeWriteTools). The name is Tractor-\n// branded and namespaced to make an accidental collision with a user's own\n// agy agent implausible; ensureAgentManifest additionally refuses to\n// overwrite a manifest at this name that lacks Tractor's marker comment.\nconst TractorAgentName = \"tractor-shell-only\"\n\n// tractorAgentMarker is a YAML comment placed at the top of every manifest\n// Tractor writes. Its presence is what makes provisioning idempotent and\n// safe: ensureAgentManifest only ever overwrites a file that already\n// carries this marker (a stale or outdated Tractor manifest); it refuses to\n// touch a same-named file that lacks it, since that means a user created\n// their own \"tractor-shell-only\" agent independently.\nconst tractorAgentMarker = \"# tractor-managed-agent: github.com/tylergannon/tractor/harness/agy — do not hand-edit\"\n\n// nativeWriteTools are the agy native tools Google's Hooks tool reference\n// documents as file-mutating operations capable of carrying ArtifactMetadata\n// (write_to_file, multi_replace_file_content) or otherwise performing native\n// in-process file writes (replace_file_content). Any of the three can\n// trigger agy's \"is not a valid artifact path\" turn failure for a target\n// outside agy's private per-conversation brain/\u003cuuid\u003e directory — the same\n// failure harness/agy's repair-retry (isArtifactPathError) recovers from\n// reactively. The manifest omits all three from its tools allowlist so the\n// model never sees them as callable, and enforceInitTools verifies that\n// invariant empirically from agy's own init event rather than trusting the\n// manifest file to still say what Tractor thinks it says.\nvar nativeWriteTools = []string{\n\t\"write_to_file\",\n\t\"replace_file_content\",\n\t\"multi_replace_file_content\",\n}\n\n// requiredTool is the tool the manifest must still expose so the model has\n// a way to create and edit workspace files: agy's shell/terminal tool.\nconst requiredTool = \"run_command\"\n\n// allowedTools is agy 1.1.15's full init.tools baseline (captured empirically\n// 2026-08-19 via `agy --output-format stream-json` with no --agent), minus\n// nativeWriteTools. It intentionally keeps every other tool agy advertises\n// by default — browser automation, MCP, subagents, scheduling, and so on —\n// so selecting the Tractor agent changes only the one thing this fix\n// targets. Because agy's `tools:` frontmatter is an allowlist, not a\n// denylist, this list does not automatically pick up tools a future agy\n// release adds; refresh it (and re-run the empirical smoke check in\n// ephemeral/worklog/20260819-agy-artifact-prevention.md) when bumping the\n// pinned agy version.\nvar allowedTools = []string{\n\t\"ask_custom_permission\",\n\t\"ask_permission\",\n\t\"ask_question\",\n\t\"browser_click_element\",\n\t\"browser_drag_pixel_to_pixel\",\n\t\"browser_get_dom\",\n\t\"browser_get_network_request\",\n\t\"browser_input\",\n\t\"browser_list_network_requests\",\n\t\"browser_mouse_down\",\n\t\"browser_mouse_up\",\n\t\"browser_move_mouse\",\n\t\"browser_press_key\",\n\t\"browser_refresh_page\",\n\t\"browser_resize_window\",\n\t\"browser_scroll\",\n\t\"browser_scroll_dom\",\n\t\"browser_select_option\",\n\t\"browser_subagent\",\n\t\"call_mcp_tool\",\n\t\"capture_browser_console_logs\",\n\t\"capture_browser_screenshot\",\n\t\"click_browser_pixel\",\n\t\"command_status\",\n\t\"define_subagent\",\n\t\"delete_knowledge\",\n\t\"execute_browser_javascript\",\n\t\"find_by_name\",\n\t\"finish\",\n\t\"generate_image\",\n\t\"grep_search\",\n\t\"invoke_subagent\",\n\t\"list_browser_pages\",\n\t\"list_dir\",\n\t\"list_permissions\",\n\t\"list_resources\",\n\t\"manage_inbox\",\n\t\"manage_subagents\",\n\t\"manage_task\",\n\t\"notebook_edit\",\n\t\"notebook_execution\",\n\t\"open_browser_url\",\n\t\"read_browser_page\",\n\t\"read_resource\",\n\t\"read_url_content\",\n\trequiredTool,\n\t\"schedule\",\n\t\"search_web\",\n\t\"sed_file\",\n\t\"send_command_input\",\n\t\"send_message\",\n\t\"view_file\",\n\t\"wait\",\n\t\"wait_5_seconds\",\n}\n\n// agentManifestPath returns the global manifest path for the Tractor agent\n// under homeDir. Global placement (~/.gemini/config/agents/\u003cname\u003e/agent.md)\n// is deliberate over a workspace-local .agents/agents/ manifest: Tractor\n// runs branches in per-branch isolated worktrees (engine/artifacts.go,\n// added in 2485e4c) each with their own workdir, so a workspace-local\n// manifest would need to be provisioned into and cleaned up from every\n// branch worktree — and a leftover file would show up in that branch's git\n// status and be swept into artifact collection. A single global manifest,\n// provisioned once and left in place, sidesteps both problems entirely and\n// is invisible to every pipeline workspace.\nfunc agentManifestPath(homeDir string) string {\n\treturn filepath.Join(homeDir, \".gemini\", \"config\", \"agents\", TractorAgentName, \"agent.md\")\n}\n\n// ensureAgentManifest idempotently provisions Tractor's custom agy agent\n// manifest under homeDir and returns the agent name to pass via --agent.\n// It is safe to call from multiple processes/adapters concurrently in the\n// sense that it always converges to the same canonical content; a lost\n// write race just means one writer's identical content wins.\nfunc ensureAgentManifest(homeDir string) (string, error) {\n\tpath := agentManifestPath(homeDir)\n\tcanonical := manifestContent()\n\texisting, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tif string(existing) == canonical {\n\t\t\treturn TractorAgentName, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !strings.Contains(string(existing), tractorAgentMarker) {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\n\t\t\t\t\"%s already exists and is not Tractor-managed (missing marker comment); \"+\n\t\t\t\t\t\"remove it or rename Tractor's agent (harness/agy.TractorAgentName) to avoid clobbering it\",\n\t\t\t\tpath,\n\t\t\t)\n\t\t}\n\t\t// A stale Tractor-managed manifest (e.g. an older allowedTools\n\t\t// baseline); fall through and overwrite with current content.\n\t} else if !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"read %s: %w\", path, err)\n\t}\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(path), 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"create %s: %w\", filepath.Dir(path), err)\n\t}\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(path, []byte(canonical), 0o644); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"write %s: %w\", path, err)\n\t}\n\treturn TractorAgentName, nil\n}\n\nfunc manifestContent() string {\n\tvar b strings.Builder\n\tb.WriteString(\"---\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(tractorAgentMarker)\n\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"name: \" + TractorAgentName + \"\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"mainAgent: true\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"subagent: false\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"description: \u003e-\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"  Tractor-provisioned agy agent. Omits agy's native file-write tools\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"  (write_to_file, replace_file_content, multi_replace_file_content) so\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"  the model cannot trigger agy's artifact-path validator, which fails a\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"  turn's successful workspace write with \\\"is not a valid artifact path\\\"\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"  whenever the target lies outside agy's private brain/\u003cuuid\u003e\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"  directory. Create and edit workspace files exclusively via\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"  run_command.\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"tools:\\n\")\n\tfor _, tool := range allowedTools {\n\t\tb.WriteString(\"  - \" + tool + \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\tb.WriteString(\"---\\n\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"Perform all workspace file creation and modification exclusively\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"through run_command (for example a shell heredoc:\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"`cat \u003e \u003cpath\u003e \u003c\u003c'EOF' ... EOF`). You do not have a native file-write\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"tool in this session; it is intentionally unavailable because it fails\\n\")\n\tb.WriteString(\"this environment's workspace writes. Do not attempt to invoke one.\\n\")\n\treturn b.String()\n}\n\n// enforceInitTools checks agy's own init event against the invariant the\n// Tractor agent manifest is supposed to establish: none of nativeWriteTools\n// advertised, requiredTool present. It runs against whatever agy actually\n// reports rather than trusting allowedTools/manifestContent, so a manifest\n// drift, an agy regression, or a misconfigured --agent flag is caught\n// before the model can wander into the broken tool and burn a turn — the\n// corroborating research report notes that an *unrecognized* tool\n// identifier in a custom agent's allowlist makes agy hang indefinitely, so\n// failing fast here on a clear mismatch is safer than discovering it via a\n// hung turn.\nfunc enforceInitTools(tools []string) error {\n\tseen := make(map[string]bool, len(tools))\n\tfor _, tool := range tools {\n\t\tseen[tool] = true\n\t}\n\tvar advertised []string\n\tfor _, forbidden := range nativeWriteTools {\n\t\tif seen[forbidden] {\n\t\t\tadvertised = append(advertised, forbidden)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif len(advertised) \u003e 0 {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\n\t\t\t\"agy advertised native write tool(s) %s despite --agent %s; \"+\n\t\t\t\t\"the manifest at ~/.gemini/config/agents/%s/agent.md no longer omits them \"+\n\t\t\t\t\"(has it been hand-edited, or does this agy version ignore tools: for a mainAgent?) — \"+\n\t\t\t\t\"delete the manifest so Tractor can re-provision it, or pin an agy version where \"+\n\t\t\t\t\"the tools: allowlist is honored\",\n\t\t\tstrings.Join(advertised, \", \"), TractorAgentName, TractorAgentName,\n\t\t)\n\t}\n\tif !seen[requiredTool] {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\n\t\t\t\"agy did not advertise %q despite --agent %s; \"+\n\t\t\t\t\"the manifest at ~/.gemini/config/agents/%s/agent.md must include it in tools: \"+\n\t\t\t\t\"or the model has no way to write workspace files — \"+\n\t\t\t\t\"delete the manifest so Tractor can re-provision it\",\n\t\t\trequiredTool, TractorAgentName, TractorAgentName,\n\t\t)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n","file_path":"/Users/tyler/src/tractor/.claude/worktrees/jovial-aryabhata-59c086/harness/agy/agent_manifest.go"},"call_id":"toolu_01G3v3Ubf4HbRd8Tiykq818u","name":"Write","node_id":"implement","ts":"2026-08-19T22:18:20.083706Z","type":"tool_call"}
