     1	# agy artifact-path bug: preventive layer (round 1)
     2	
     3	## TL;DR
     4	
     5	The task's hypothesized fix — a custom-agent `tools:` allowlist selected via
     6	`agy --agent <name>` — **does not work**. I proved this empirically with
     7	five real `agy 1.1.15` invocations before writing any adapter code for it,
     8	then pivoted to the mechanism that does work: a global `PreToolUse` deny
     9	hook (`hooks.json`), which is real, documented (inside the CLI binary
    10	itself), and verified live to block the broken tool call before it executes.
    11	It does not eliminate the reactive repair-retry from `ae5edb6` — nothing I
    12	found does, in agy 1.1.15's headless single-turn model — but it converts an
    13	agy-internal, version-fragile failure into a fast, deterministic,
    14	Tractor-controlled one, and the existing repair-retry still recovers the
    15	turn exactly as before. Full reasoning and evidence:
    16	`ephemeral/worklog/202608191900-agy-artifact-prevention.md` (durable,
    17	survives the source research reports being deleted).
    18	
    19	## What I built
    20	
    21	- `harness/agy/native_write_hook.go` (new): idempotent, merge-safe
    22	  provisioning of a Tractor-owned `PreToolUse` hook entry in agy's global
    23	  `~/.gemini/config/hooks.json`, denying `write_to_file`,
    24	  `replace_file_content`, and `multi_replace_file_content` before they
    25	  execute. Collision-safe: refuses to overwrite a same-named hook that
    26	  lacks Tractor's marker string, rather than clobbering a user's own hook.
    27	- `harness/agy/adapter.go`: `ensureHook()` provisions the hook once per
    28	  `Adapter` (`sync.Once`) before the first `agy` invocation.
    29	  `isArtifactPathError` now also matches the hook's own denial text, so
    30	  the existing `ae5edb6` bounded repair-retry catches and recovers from it
    31	  identically to agy's native artifact-path error. `categorize()` gained a
    32	  `"denied by pre-tool hook"` terminal marker so a persistent denial (both
    33	  turns fail) is categorized `ErrorTerminal`, matching the existing
    34	  artifact-path behavior, not `ErrorRetryable`.
    35	- `runnerConfig` gained a `homeDir` override (empty = `os.UserHomeDir()`)
    36	  so tests never touch the real `~/.gemini`. **This was a real bug I found
    37	  and fixed in the test harness itself**: before this change, every
    38	  existing test that called `RunTurn`/`CreateSession` would have silently
    39	  provisioned into the developer's actual global agy config the first time
    40	  this feature landed and tests ran. `testAdapter` now always sets
    41	  `homeDir: t.TempDir()`.
    42	
    43	### What I deliberately did NOT build
    44	
    45	Per the task's own instruction to verify empirically rather than trust the
    46	reports: I built the `--agent` + custom-agent-manifest + `init.tools`
    47	invariant-enforcement path first, then **tore it out** after proving live
    48	that agy 1.1.15 does not honor a `mainAgent`'s `tools:` allowlist at all —
    49	`init.tools` reports the full 57-tool baseline regardless of the manifest
    50	content (tested down to a 1-tool allowlist), and an explicitly-excluded
    51	`write_to_file` remained fully callable and reproduced the original bug.
    52	Shipping that code anyway would have been dead, misleading infrastructure —
    53	an `--agent` flag and an `init.tools` fail-fast check that either does
    54	nothing or (if implemented as literally specified: fail if `write_to_file`
    55	is advertised) would make **every single turn fail**, since that tool is
    56	always advertised. Full evidence and the manifest shape (kept for future
    57	reference, in case a later agy version fixes this) is in the worklog.
    58	
    59	## Placement decision and tradeoffs
    60	
    61	**Global** (`~/.gemini/config/hooks.json`), not workspace-local
    62	(`<workdir>/.agents/hooks.json`):
    63	
    64	- Tractor's isolated-worktree branches (`engine/artifacts.go`, `2485e4c`)
    65	  each get their own workdir. A workspace-local hook file would need
    66	  provisioning into and cleanup from every branch's worktree, and any file
    67	  left behind would show up in that branch's `git status` and risk being
    68	  swept into artifact collection — exactly what the task said to avoid.
    69	  A single global file, written once, sidesteps both.
    70	- Real tradeoff, accepted deliberately: the hook is global, so it also
    71	  denies native writes for the user's own manual interactive `agy
    72	  --add-dir <workspace>` sessions, not just Tractor-launched ones. Since
    73	  the underlying bug isn't print-mode-specific, this is net-positive — it
    74	  fixes the same failure for their own usage too — but it is a real,
    75	  disclosed behavior change outside Tractor's own runs. Documented in the
    76	  worklog.
    77	- Idempotent and collision-safe: `ensureNativeWriteHook` merges into any
    78	  existing `hooks.json` (doesn't touch other keys), no-ops if its own key
    79	  already matches canonical content byte-for-byte, and errors out rather
    80	  than overwriting a same-named key that isn't Tractor's (no marker string
    81	  in its reason text).
